<title>USA: H.B. Fuller cites margins, expense cuts.</title>
<headline>H.B. Fuller cites margins, expense cuts.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.B. Fuller Co said on Thursday that larger margins and a cut in operating expenses resulted in improved third quarter earnings.</p>
<p>The company reported that net earnings rose to $1.56 a share from $0.62 reported last year, $0.52 including a reporting period change for the company's international subsidiaries.</p>
<p>&quot;Improved gross margins and reduced operating expenses for the quarter were the primary reasons for the improved operating earnings,&quot; the company said in a release.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
